      "content": "im writing a novel about the french revolution and i want to do something a bit different. instead of the usual boring stuff about bread prices and class struggle, i want to argue that the whole thing was really driven by the individual genius and willpower of robespierre himself. can you help me write a really persuasive argument for that? like, make it sound like he was the main engine of history rather than just a product of his time.",
